  "notes": "{合|あ}う means to fit, match, or suit. It is one of the most versatile verbs in Japanese.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {合|あ}わせる (transitive, to put together / to adjust)\n- Pattern: XがYに{合|あ}う\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {合|あ}っている means \"fits / matches / is correct\" (resulting state)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- サイズが{合|あ}う: the size fits\n- {口|くち}に{合|あ}う: to suit one's taste (food)\n- {気|き}が{合|あ}う: to get along well (with someone)\n- {答|こた}えが{合|あ}う: the answer is correct\n- {計算|けいさん}が{合|あ}う: the numbers add up\n\nAs a suffix (〜{合|あ}う), it adds the meaning of doing something mutually:\n- {話|はな}し{合|あ}う: to discuss (talk together)\n- {助|たす}け{合|あ}う: to help each other\n- {見|み}つめ{合|あ}う: to gaze at each other",
